  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 351,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Systemic therapy for a blood cancer: hit EVERY dividing cell, or ONE target on the tumour?",
   "lines": [
    "surgery only DIAGNOSES (resect a node) · radiation treats locally: see the RADIATION ONCOLOGY chart",
    "glucocorticoids (prednisone, dexamethasone) kill lymphoid cells: lymphomas, chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), acute B-cell leukemia, myeloma · also shrink swelling around metastases"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_cyt",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 892,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "CLASSIC cytotoxic: every dividing cell",
   "lines": [
    "every one: myelosuppression (infection), hair loss, mucositis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_tar",
   "x": 977,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "TARGETED and IMMUNE: one molecule",
   "lines": [
    "chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) T cells: the patient's own, modified → relapsed acute lymphoblastic leukemia (< 26 y), relapsed diffuse large B-cell lymphoma"
   ]
  },
